            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of spontaneous coronary dissection with drug-eluting stents--late clinical, angiographic and IVUS follow up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E93-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prognosis of spontaneous coronary artery dissection is uncertain and optimal treatment is unknown. We previously described the first reported implantation of drug-eluting stents in spontaneous coronary artery dissection. The immediate angiographic result was good, and we now report the late clinical, angiographic and intravascular ultrasound follow up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
